&lt;p&gt;We are the Data Visualization team, a core part of the AI/BI organization. Our mission is to enable everyone in an organization to make intelligent business decisions informed by the best data available. We empower business teams via self-service analytics, helping them author high-quality visualizations and dashboards using our AI-first authoring experience. We own the visualization library, the dashboarding canvas, and the agentic authoring workflows that bridge the gap between complex data and actionable insights.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking a dedicated Engineering Leader for our Data Visualization team in Bellevue. This team is responsible for the entire life cycle of visual insights: from the underlying visualization framework (using technologies like React and Vega-Lite) to building advanced features like field variables, drill-downs, and AI-driven chart generation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will report directly to the Senior Manager of Engineering.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lead a Talented Team:&lt;/strong&gt; You will lead a high-performing engineering team in Bellevue focused on revolutionizing how users visualize data with AI/BI Dashboards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Talent Development:&lt;/strong&gt; You will oversee the sustained recruitment of top-tier frontend and visualization talent and foster a culture of mentorship and professional growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strategic Execution:&lt;/strong&gt; You will build processes to implement the AI/BI product vision, focusing on &quot;BI Takeout&quot; initiatives to replace legacy tools with superior Databricks-native experiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Operational Excellence:&lt;/strong&gt; You will ensure the visualization platform is not only feature-rich but also high-performing, reliable, and easy to operate.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technical Stewardship:&lt;/strong&gt; You will manage technical debt (e.g., framework migrations, performance optimizations) while balancing an ambitious roadmap that includes agentic authoring and semantic model integration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We Look For&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Frontend Expertise:&lt;/strong&gt; 5+ years of hands-on experience in web frontend development, with a strong preference for React-based applications and modern state management (e.g., MobX).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Management Experience:&lt;/strong&gt; 2+ years leading and managing high-performing engineering teams, ideally in a fast-paced product environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Visualization Passion:&lt;/strong&gt; A deep interest in data visualization, charting libraries (e.g., D3.js, Vega-Lite), or UX for complex data tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Efficiency Driver:&lt;/strong&gt; Proven ability to drive technical initiatives that improve team productivity, such as optimizing CI/CD runtimes or streamlining visualization frameworks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Talent Magnet:&lt;/strong&gt; A strong track record of attracting, hiring, and retaining top engineering talent, including the ability to mentor engineers at various levels.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Collaborative Leader:&lt;/strong&gt; Experience working with cross-functional stakeholders including Product Management, Design, and AI Research teams to deliver agentic product experiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Adaptability:&lt;/strong&gt; Resilience in a rapidly evolving tech environment, with the ability to pivot priorities based on customer feedback and emerging AI capabilities.&lt;/li&gt;
