&lt;p&gt;While candidates in the listed location(s) are encouraged for this role, candidates in other locations will be considered.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Databricks is seeking a Real Estate Strategic Planning Lead to join our Real Estate &amp;amp; Workplace Services (REWS) team. Reporting to Global Real Estate Strategy &amp;amp; Transactions, this highly visible and impactful role will be responsible for portfolio planning, scenario planning, and portfolio optimization across Databricks’ global real estate portfolio. The role will support executive decision-making through strategic analysis, financial modeling, and business case support to inform key real estate decisions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;2006&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-renderer-mark=&quot;true&quot;&gt;The impact you will have: &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Finance and Real Estate Leadership to maintain REWS long-range portfolio plan&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create and maintain flexible portfolio models and manage complex scenario planning initiatives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop portfolio optimization recommendations aligned with business growth, financial objectives, and employee experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct financial, operational, and portfolio analyses to support strategic real estate decision-making&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support development of executive-ready business cases, presentations, and strategic recommendations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate complex portfolio tradeoffs into clear, data-driven insights and actionable recommendations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and maintain recurring portfolio reporting, dashboards, and key performance metrics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct ad hoc analyses and decision support for high-priority REWS cross-functional initiatives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Finance, Workplace, People, IT, and Real Estate stakeholders globally to support portfolio planning initiatives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help establish scalable planning frameworks, reporting standards, and governance processes as Databricks continues to grow&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;2367&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-renderer-mark=&quot;true&quot;&gt;What we look for:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in Real Estate, Finance, Economics, Business Administration, or a related field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years of experience in a combination of Real Estate, Finance, Strategy, Management Consulting, or related fields with a track record of success&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent analytical skills, including financial modeling, forecasting, portfolio analysis, and scenario planning&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional problem-solving skills with demonstrated ability to structure complex problems and develop solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong presentation, verbal, and written communication skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to manage multiple high-visibility projects simultaneously in a fast-paced environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in a results-driven, solutions-oriented environment with competing priorities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong collaboration skills and ability to work effectively across cross-functional stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced proficiency in Google Sheets, Excel, and presentation development&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with planning and reporting tools such as Anaplan, Tableau, Databricks, or similar platforms preferred&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
