&lt;p&gt;Databricks is looking for a talented and experienced Senior Corporate Counsel to join our expanding Legal team.&amp;nbsp; This position will report to our Senior Managing Counsel, Corporate, and is a unique opportunity to advise on and drive a broad range of corporate matters, including governance, M&amp;amp;A and venture transactions, public company readiness and securities law compliance and subsidiary management, and to provide business-focused legal advice to stakeholders throughout Databricks on a daily basis.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will be agile, highly organized and have the skills, drive and flexibility to support and accelerate a leading technology company, addressing novel legal issues and organizational challenges.&amp;nbsp; A successful candidate will be a resourceful self-starter, comfortable working in a fast-paced and dynamic environment and excellent at building strong relationships.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support all phases of corporate transactions, including M&amp;amp;A, ventures and equity and capital raising transactions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support public company readiness and securities law compliance initiatives&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop, implement and continuously improve disclosure controls and procedures in coordination with finance, investor relations and other internal stakeholders&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare and review board and committee materials and advise on board-related governance matters&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare governance and compliance policies and procedures, including updates to such policies and procedures&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review and advise internal stakeholders with respect to investor presentations, offering materials, public announcements, press releases, and other corporate communications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support ESG and sustainability reporting initiatives as needed, with a focus on corporate-governance, disclosure and public-company reporting considerations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advise on antitrust and competition law aspects of M&amp;amp;A, as well as provide global antitrust and competition counseling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead international subsidiary management, including formation and maintenance of domestic and international subsidiaries&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish and execute OKRs to continuously improve processes for scaling legal support for general corporate matters&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and maintain relationships with internal and external stakeholders, including finance, corporate development, marketing, investor relations and outside counsel&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
